From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] Input: oneplus-pogo-kbd: add the Lenovo TB375FC keyboard

The keyboard cover of the Lenovo Xiaoxin Pad Pro 12.7 (TB375FC) and the
Idea Tab Pro (TB373FU) is also built around a Tinno keyboard MCU on a
half-duplex 921600 8N1 UART, with the same gate on the host TX and the
same timing, but it speaks an older form of the protocol. The commands
carry largely the same things under other numbers, and the frames look
different:

  55 x8 | 25 | cmd | e(len) | e(payload[len]) | e(sum) | 2C | 55 x4

e() turns a byte into two symbols, one per nibble, through one of eight
substitution rows that the sender picks at random for each frame. The
rows share no symbols, so the first symbol tells the receiver the row.
sum is the low byte of the sum of all bytes from the 25 up to e(sum), in
place of the CRC16, and a resent frame starts with 26. There are no
addresses, so an echo is told by its command.

The rest differs as well:

- Commands: 0x61 keys, 0x62 consumer keys, 0x63 touchpad, 0x6A
  parameters, 0x7B sync and 0x92 general. A reply is still the command
  plus one.
- Keys are the modifiers and six usages, without the reserved byte of a
  boot report. The consumer usages are the same.
- The touchpad has four fingers and reports in 2944x1840, a button byte
  first, and bit 0 of the finger flags says down. A finger left out has
  been lifted.
- A hall sensor on a GPIO tells about attach and detach, so there are no
  heartbeats to watch and the wire need not be sampled. Any frame after
  power on means the keyboard is up.
- The RX pin leaves the UART while the keyboard is off, as nothing
  drives the wire then, and returns 30 ms after the supply is on.
- The wake line is used for system wakeup only, on its rising edge.
- The caps lock LED is parameter 0x27.

Select all this with the compatible through a table of what differs
between the two forms. The per-compatible CRC seed that the OnePlus
MT6897 tablets would need is not added, as nothing here uses it.

The keyboard also pushes its enable state: 0x93, sub-command 3, with 0
when it has turned its keys and touchpad off and 1 when it is back. The
stock driver passes that on as two keys. The tablet has no sensor of its
own for the keyboard folded back behind it, so this should be that, and
the driver reports it as SW_TABLET_MODE on an input device of its own.
It also reports tablet mode without a keyboard, as
surface_aggregator_tabletsw does.

That frame is lost if it comes while the UART sleeps, so a key or a
finger going down turns tablet mode off as well. A release does not, as
the keyboard may send one after it has turned off. The other way round
nothing tells: a keyboard folded during system sleep shows only if it
sends its state again after the wake notification, which is to be seen
on the hardware.

All of this comes from the stock tn_keyboard module of the tablet (GPL,
source not released, ZUI 17.0.04.266), which still has its symbols. It
has not been tried on the hardware, as the tablet is not unlocked yet.
The stock driver also has a backlight (parameter 0x23), an Fn lock
(0x2A), the touchpad off (0x21), the mute and microphone LEDs (0x28,
0x29) and cuts the keyboard supply 60 s after the cover closes. None of
those are here yet.

